4. Project Cost Management   -   Includes the processes involved in planning, 
estimating, budgeting, financing, funding, managing, and controlling costs so the 
project can be completed within the approved budget. 
5 . Project Procurement Management   -   Includes the processes necessary to 
purchase or acquire products, services, or results needed from outside the 
project team 
3. Explain the elements of a Project Charter. 
Project purpose; 
1. Measurable project objectives and related success criteria; 
2. High - level requirements; 
3. High - level project description, boundaries, and key deliverables; 
4.   Overall project risk; 
5. Summary milestone schedule; 
6. Preapproved financial resources; 
7. Key stakeholder list; 
8. Project approval requirements (i.e., what constitutes project success, who 
the   project is successful, and who signs off on the project); 
9. Project exit criteria (i.e., what are the conditions to be met in order to close or 
to cancel 
the project or phase); 
10. Assigned project manager, responsibility, and authority level; and 
11. Name and authority of the sponsor or other person(s) authorizing the 
project charter
